# Expectation record for 05_pointers/008_array_decay_parameters.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 008_array_decay_parameters
area               = 05_pointers
description        = Array-to-pointer decay in parameter position, including two- and three-dimensional arrays and an array of pointers
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every function reads only as many elements as the caller guarantees exist: the element count
passed is never larger than the array it accompanies, the row and plane counts never exceed
3 and 2, and each inner bound is fixed by the parameter type itself.  Passing the address of
an interior element together with the count of elements that remain keeps every access in
bounds, and the zero-count call performs no access at all.  first_after_step advances its
parameter by a step smaller than the element count, so the object it then reads exists.
The pointer table holds four pointers to distinct elements of one_d, all non-null, so no null
pointer is dereferenced.  The flattened index is built from a difference taken in the OUTER
array of rows, where a and a + row designate elements of one and the same object, scaled by
the row width taken from the parameter type; element pointers belonging to two different
inner arrays are never subtracted, which pointer subtraction would not permit even though the
enclosing two-dimensional array is contiguous.  The row and column arguments are checked
against the bounds before use, so a + row is never advanced more than one element past the
last row.  The pointer one past the end of a row is formed and differenced but never
dereferenced, which is exactly what the standard permits.
No signed integer overflow, no shift out of range, no aliasing violation, no read of
uninitialized storage, no object modified twice between sequence points, at most one
side-effecting argument per call, and no dependence on padding bytes or on the relative
addresses of unrelated objects.
Every decay shape here is exercised a second time with its element counts and indices taken
from volatile-qualified storage, so the constant folder's answer cannot stand in for the one
the backend computes at run time.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.  printf is the only external symbol; no file,
socket, environment variable, clock or random source is touched, and every input is a literal
in this source file.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
sizeof of a decayed parameter is pointer width, which is 4 on i686 and 8 on the other three
targets, so it is never printed.  Element counts are computed at the caller, where the array
type is still intact, and are printed as ratios of the form sizeof arr / sizeof arr[0], which
are dimensionless and identical on all four targets.  Row strides and element spans are
printed as element counts, never as byte counts.
No address or pointer value is printed.  Pointer facts appear only as element-scaled
differences and as the index values derived from them, and every pointer difference is cast to
long long before printing, so the printed text is identical whether ptrdiff_t is 32 or 64 bits
wide.  No plain char object appears anywhere in the program, so the measured plain-char
signedness difference between the targets cannot reach it.  The only conversion specifiers
used anywhere are %d and %lld, both of which are independent of target width.
Because no implementation-defined width reaches the printed text, the width difference is
neutralized by construction rather than by narrowing coverage: the full four-target matrix,
all three optimization levels and all three oracles stay enabled for this program.  This
paragraph is the durable record of that, so a later maintainer does not restrict the target
list in the belief that a decayed parameter's pointer width forces it.
END
